# TUI-DESIGN-5 §3 / §10 (slot R5-3): `/context` then `/compact` under `--mock` at 120x40, plus the
# `nothing to compact` branch and the `compaction is off` branch. Hermetic: `--mock` only, no network, no key.
#
# STATUS — this file does not run yet, and that is a dependency, not a skip.
#   `/context` and `/compact` are §9.2's W4 rows on `src/tui/commands/registry.ts` (owner R5-2) and their handlers
#   are R5-1's `src/cli/session.ts` arms (both hunks are written verbatim in R5-3's report). Until those two PRs
#   land, `send /context` types a line the palette refuses, so the scenario asserts nothing. It is committed now,
#   with the rows below, so the integrator has the scenario in hand the day the commands resolve — TD4 §14.2
#   finding 41's "never a dead command" defect is exactly what an absent scenario lets back in.
#
# run-smoke.sh needs three rows for this scenario; they belong to R5-2 (§9.2 gives it `test/pty/**` in W5):
#   env    : r5-context) extra_env="$extra_env JEVCODE_CONTEXT_COMPACTION=code";;
#   check  : r5-context) grep -q 'context [·-] ' "$txt" && checks="$checks r5-context:block" || { ok=0; checks="$checks MISSING:r5-context-block"; }
#   select : sel_named r5-context && run r5-context 0 40 120 chat --mock
#
# What it proves, beyond "it renders":
#   - §3.2's three reads join into ONE block whose head is S48 and whose first row is `formatBudget`'s own text;
#   - §3.7's rungs: the per-file table with its reason column at 120 and 80, the count row alone at 40;
#   - §3.3: `/compact` on a two-step history answers S57 and the `off` run answers S58a — never the other way;
#   - §3.4: the engine's own `compaction:` notice is unchanged and the `─ compaction ─` rule sits ABOVE it;
#   - G-R5-9: `assertNoKeyBytes` over every frame (the block prints paths and byte counts, never a key).

expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.4

# 1 — `/context` before any run: §7 row 36's own sentence, not an empty block
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect no run is live
sleep 0.3
mark context-no-run

# 2 — a run, so `status().context` exists; `--mock` steps are deterministic
send do a thing
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 1.2
mark run-live

# 3 — the full block at 120x40: the head, `budget`, `recent steps`, `files in view` and the per-file table
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect context [·-] step
sleep 0.4
mark context-120

# 4 — the 40-column rung: the same head, the count row, and NO per-file rows (§3.7)
resize 40 40
sleep 0.8
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 0.4
mark context-40

# 5 — the 80-column rung: the per-file rows are back and the reason column survives (§3.7, §14.2 finding 1)
resize 40 80
sleep 0.8
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 0.4
mark context-80

# 6 — `/compact` with one step in history: S57, and NEVER the `off` sentence on a `code` run
resize 40 120
sleep 0.6
send /compact
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect nothing to compact
sleep 0.3
mark compact-nothing

send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
